HTML Microdata is a specification used to embed structured data directly into HTML content. It helps search engines better understand webpage information by adding meaningful metadata to HTML elements.

Uses predefined attributes to describe items and their properties.
Helps search engines interpret content more accurately.
Enables enhanced search results like rich snippets and knowledge panels.
Improves SEO visibility and content understanding.




